     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, 1000 mg daily is five times the labeled maximum, and I don't know of any accepted protocol for it. Failure of standard dosing is normally handled by switching or augmenting therapy, not by dosing far above the ceiling. The risk of serious harm, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity, is high enough that I'd want a second check before this reaches the patient.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Pharmacy and attending review.** Have the prescriber and a clinical pharmacist confirm the dose. If they approve, it can be entered through their override pathway, with their documentation attached.\n- **A different dose.** If you want to enter a dose within the standard range, such as 200 mg daily, I can do that right away.\n- **Other options.** I can help you write up the question for the specialist or pharmacy, for example about switching agents, augmentation, or therapeutic drug monitoring."
      }
